# The second mission's mask ship and the ships that fly with it: the Asp that carries the masking device, and the
# Constrictor and the Cougar, which nothing else spawns. It starts from mask-mission.cdr (Tools/PrepareCommanders.py):
# the fighter (a military laser, ECM, an energy unit, 20 kills) briefed for the mission at Lave and docked at Leesti
# a jump later, where the mission ships spawn as soon as he launches. The first launch after the boot dies at once:
# PlaceAtSpawnPoint turns the spawn point by the sine and cosine pairs the last ComputeVelocity left (rotationSinCos
# 6 and 7), nothing has set them since the boot, and at zero they put the spawn point on the player, so the escorts,
# scattered round it, ram him. GAME OVER, then a new game, and the same commander, 3,680,037 random draws on
# (mask-mission-fight.cdr), is copied in and loaded mid-replay: this time the ships spawn 10,000 units out. Two are
# destroyed, and the mission ship spawned in each one's place is first a Constrictor, then a Cougar. The draw count
# was found by a search over counts; the fight was played by a scratch program that steered at the nearest ship each
# frame and fired when it was in the sights, and what it pressed is recorded here.
file JAMESON.CDR mask-mission.cdr
wait 0.5; key space; wait 3.5      # any key: the credits, then the status screen
key Escape; wait 0.3               # the disc menu
key l; wait 0.3                    # Load Commander: it asks for a file name
key j; key a; key m; key e; key s; key o; key n; key Return; wait 0.5
